// A compatible tracked framebuffer already detected real CPU writes
// above using RAMHash/uploadRAM and reports them as fbChangesMade.
// Its changed raw bytes can also be our own fullSync GPU writeback.
// Treating that as a second screen event presents the old VI buffer
// before the guest swaps it, and contaminates the VI rate factors.
// Keep raw-hash detection for untracked or uncovered VI memory;
// VI changes and genuine tracked CPU updates still present normally.
const bool trackedVIRange = (screenFb != nullptr) && (screenFb->RAMBytes >= screenFbBytes);
screenChangesMade = !trackedVIRange && (newScreenHash != lastScreenHash);
